## How to use

1. Ask the orchestrator for the build lock (post `REQUEST` on the board).
2. Write your agent id and the current time into the `Holder` / `Granted at` fields below.
3. Run your build / test / e2e commands.
4. Paste the **raw output** into `docs/phase2/handoffs/<ID>.md`.
5. Reset the fields to `FREE` and release.

Only one agent may hold this lock at a time. `npm run build`, `npm run build:packages`,
`npm run build:studio`, `npm run test:unit` and `npx playwright test` all require it.
`npx tsc --noEmit` and single-file `npx vitest run <file>` do not.

## Why it exists

During Phase 1 the host reached load average **161–189** with ~16 MB free RAM. Under that load
vitest workers timed out, whole test files failed to collect with **no assertion**, and the
failing set **changed on every run** (2 → 4 → 3 failures). Freeing the host restored the stable
result. A suite run that disagrees with the previous run is a **load symptom, not a code
symptom**, until proven otherwise.
